    "result_text": "All 9 test classes ran (17 tests total), all green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment rule formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` following standard Spring conventions across the layers:\n\n**Domain** \u2014 `model/Owner.java`: added a `customerCode` field mapped to the `customer_code` column, with getter/setter.\n\n**Service** \u2014 `service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`: in `saveOwner(...)`, a new owner without a code gets one assigned via a private `generateCustomerCode` helper:\n- **LAST3** = first three letters of `lastName`, upper-cased (guarded for short names).\n- **NNNN** = `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1`, zero-padded to 4 digits (`String.format(\"%s-%04d\", ...)`) \u2014 a global sequence equal to one more than the current owner count.\n- Only applied when the owner is new and has no code, so updates/re-saves don't mutate it.\n\n**API contract** \u2014 `resources/openapi.yml`: added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` string on the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in `GET /api/owners/{id}` responses (MapStruct maps it automatically by name).\n\n**Persistence** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to all four schema files (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres), and appended the trailing seed value to the column-less `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)` statements in the hsqldb and mysql `data.sql` files (h2/postgres already use explicit column lists).\n\n**Verification** \u2014 `Cp09Tests` passes (e.g. `SMI-0011`/`JON-0012` with the global sequence incrementing by one), and the full suite is green: **17 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**.",
